# tt_bot v2.3 Engineering Rules

## Architecture & Security Invariants
- Never bypass `EndpointProber` / `_SafeResolver` anti-rebinding SSRF protection unless `ALLOW_PRIVATE_ENDPOINTS=true` is explicitly set.
- Every task or log query/mutation in `src/database.py` and `src/handlers.py` MUST enforce ownership via `user_id` (IDOR guard).
- Every user-controlled string rendered with `parse_mode="HTML"` MUST pass through `html.escape()`.
- Every CSV export MUST neutralize formula prefixes (`=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, `\t`, `\r`) via `_sanitize_csv_cell()`.
- Every inline button `callback_data` in `src/keyboards.py` MUST have a matching handler in `src/handlers.py`.
- Keep `ThrottleMiddleware` registered on messages and callbacks, and keep `fallback_message` registered LAST on `router`.

## Code Quality & Offline CI
- Keep McCabe complexity `<= 10` (`flake8 --max-complexity=10 --max-line-length=120`).
- Format with `black --line-length=88 src tests`.
- All pytest tests MUST run strictly offline with `--allow-hosts=127.0.0.1,::1 --allow-unix-socket` and maintain `>= 90%` coverage on `src/`.

## Frontend (`docs/`)
- Preserve the strict tactile notebook + blueprint identity defined in `docs/DESIGN.md` (hard 2px borders, index tabs, ⌘K command palette, toasts, Zero-CLS static HTML, no React bundler).
- Keep SEO metadata (`canonical`, `og:url`, `og:image`, `twitter:card`, single `<h1>`, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`) valid on every page.
